{"id": "EUVD-2026-86191", "enisaUuid": "54ac54fa-815e-383f-8002-43a2d8b6cc07", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: ibss: wait for in-flight TX on disconnect\n\nWhile leaving an IBSS in ieee80211_ibss_disconnect() mac80211 flushes\nstations, turns the carrier off and immediately tells the driver to\nleave as well. While there may be synchronize_net() in station flush\nand in this code later, packets can still be transmitted due to\ncross-CPU race conditions after carrier off is set.\nTherefore, it's possible for a race to happen where a TX to the\ndriver occurs while or after telling it to leave the IBSS. This can\nbe confusing to drivers, and in the case of iwlwifi leads to an\nattempt to use invalid queues.\n\nMove netif_carrier_off() to occur before sta_info_flush() during\nIBSS disconnect, and add synchronize_net() if flushing didn't,\nso that the synchronize_net() always happens between turning the\ncarrier off and telling the driver, avoiding this race.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:02:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:39", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8e4a07ed82bae5d13525770880dc6dfd27f9bccd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/20a3fb5e1a95caa34896853ca17a50d21c754969", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b3451e6971248250312ad32dd7f63cc9f0a925f5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d0e69d9afa59b93c30294eba89b1f15f69e91105"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93804", "GHSA-f3pr-77p4-f6r5"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "321cf602-c1bc-36f0-ab4f-18221daebc9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "48fe759d-5ccd-38aa-b71c-cfd6674bc1e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "4e3bb1e5-4c97-3a7e-87cd-37c143d848de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.3"}, {"id": "61342a87-b38d-36d4-9253-25927c12b147", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "86a2ea4134b48f6371103cfceb521bf2d2bf76cd <20a3fb5e1a95caa34896853ca17a50d21c754969"}, {"id": "7dc4df5b-787f-3c5b-b2af-31de70b344ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "86a2ea4134b48f6371103cfceb521bf2d2bf76cd <d0e69d9afa59b93c30294eba89b1f15f69e91105"}, {"id": "862a6010-025c-3f3a-8a84-f4110e7d3001", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a610cf82-9f22-31e9-81cc-cdb1cfa44f19", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "adf004c9-6c01-3d68-843b-31c0f2ac7392", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "d8205ed0-dde9-348a-b89f-6cba05161bf0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "86a2ea4134b48f6371103cfceb521bf2d2bf76cd <8e4a07ed82bae5d13525770880dc6dfd27f9bccd"}, {"id": "d8758446-4806-3da3-a2e2-17318b6ddb57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "86a2ea4134b48f6371103cfceb521bf2d2bf76cd <b3451e6971248250312ad32dd7f63cc9f0a925f5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "678723d8-c540-3945-bc08-5e8ca55aba28", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}